+# ExecPlan: GFX-01-02 isolated settings candidate
+
+## Goal
+An executable tested settings-v2-candidate and pure adaptive controller bound to 17b1, with finite local runner handoff.
+
+## Context
+Read task package 00/01/03/common contract/card/Goal, GFX sections 6-9/11, REG X-02/X-03/G-01/G-02, AGENTS.md, .agent/PLANS.md, current prototype and planning audit. Product sources are apps/weltraum-browser/src/settings/** and render/three/graphicsSettingsAdapter.ts. The original module and its tests are frozen as a control; the changed snapshot carries the same store API. No general graphics engine or second active store.
+
+## Non-goals
+Product integration, world/solver/save/debris changes, resource ledger, feature rendering, GPU benchmarks, dependency upgrades of the product, commit/push.
+
+## Architecture decision
+Keep mature settings validation/presets/storage/controller, extend snapshot files only. Pure quality code imports no Three. Capability data is scalar, bounded and copied from renderer context/device; no probe canvas. Browser uses one small WebGL2 renderer context for functional probe demonstration, no heavy native/GPU pilot. User desire is serialized; transient scale/DPR lives solely in current/state and is never fed back into draft. A0 S3 owns resource admission.
+
+## Implementation phases
+1. Freeze source/control and run unchanged tests; add red v2/controller oracles.
+2. Extend module with strict v1 migration; implement bounded telemetry and pure policy.
+3. Probe actual context and implement small DOM UI; functional browser smoke.
+4. Typecheck/build/tests, read-only review and scope/source checks.
+5. Freeze bytes/digests, finite runner profile, README/REPORT/HANDOFF/receipt and exact review diff.
+
+## Tests and evidence
+Original unit control, focused v2 negative/transaction tests, full golden decision sequences, probe missing/invalid cases, Node22 typecheck and compiled browser serving, tool-native browser keyboard/manual-limit smoke and screenshots. Outputs under tests/; new dependencies pinned in spike only with integrity/license/export evidence. No Unity runtime code changes; Unity checks are not applicable.
+
+## Risks
+Old strict envelope validation rejects future versions; future bytes must be preserved. Missing timers prevent attribution, never imply spare GPU capacity. Browser name is not proof of a preferred adapter. Concurrent load prevents reference qualification.
+
+## Rollback / safe stop
+Keep product tree unchanged. Preserve raw failures. Material unknown contracts are escalated, absent target hardware only limits its evidence. No task completion before real verification/preflight.
+
+## Progress log
+- [x] Fixed isolated clean baseline created.
+- [x] Bound control and new red oracle.
+- [x] Candidate/controller/probe/UI implemented.
+- [x] Verification and review: 74/74, typecheck/build, actual browser smoke/negative cases; no open read-only findings.
+- [x] Bound handoff: receipt/repro/export authored; exact scope and built bytes sealed and verified with exit 0. Final seal is regenerated after task closure.
+
+## Definition of done
+Independent runnable obligations pass; missing integrated/hardware obligations enumerated. Receipt separates implementation, code/oracle, environment, hardware, adoption and product integration. Complete dirty-tree/source/lock/input bindings are verifiable. No fabricated approvals.
+
+## Verification boundary
+Inherited DevToolbox product typecheck fails MODULE_NOT_FOUND because product node_modules is absent and read-only. Specs pass; own typecheck/build/unit/browser evidence passes. Completion preflight is advisory with no blockers; focused scope evidence is accepted for task completion, preserving global failure. Hardware/reference and integrated Hestia proof remain NOT_RUN.
