+# Capability: additive settings and bounded adaptive resolution
+
+## Requirements
+
+- The existing settings module SHALL remain the sole store. All 19 original IDs and preset/effects semantics SHALL survive migration from envelope v1 to v2. V2 SHALL add rayTracing, weatherQuality, powerPreference and adaptiveResolution with manual scale/DPR limits and target FPS. No runtime handles or effective values SHALL serialize.
+- Ray/weather pipelines absent from the renderer SHALL report Planned/Unsupported. Capabilities SHALL be queried through the existing renderer/context, with actual backend/adapter, optional timer/features/limits and unknown memory explicit. Probing SHALL NOT create a second canvas or classify speed by device name. Power changes SHALL require renderer restart.
+- BoundedFrameWindow SHALL retain finite bounded samples and expose p50/p95 plus validity. The pure decideQuality(metrics, desired, current, state) SHALL lower renderScale before DPR on sustained measured GPU pressure, respect cooldown/hysteresis/manual limits, and report CPU pressure without repeatedly reducing pixels.
+- Missing/invalid/disjoint sensors, hidden tab, warmup, stale/out-of-order windows and reference freeze SHALL prevent automatic changes. Capability/manual-limit changes SHALL clamp only effective quality. Stable inputs SHALL have identical full decision sequences. World/source/save/collision identity SHALL remain untouched.
+- Apply/cancel/storage failure/runtime failure/restart behavior SHALL be covered without removing historical assertions. The browser UI SHALL load actual v1 settings and display draft/confirmed/effective/capability separately, allow keyboard operation and enforce manual limits.
+
+## Scenarios
+
+1. V1 preset/custom preferences migrate without changing old values; malformed/future envelopes fail closed and cannot be silently overwritten.
+2. A short spike or alternating pressure does not change resolution; sustained GPU load steps down, long reserve steps up within limits; CPU load does not step down.
+3. noGPU/noAdapter/noTimer/unknownMemory, hidden/visible changes and cold shader windows never fabricate zero-time headroom.
+4. Failed persistence leaves confirmed/runtime unchanged; failed runtime apply is reported and desired versus effective remain visibly separate; cancel restores the confirmed draft.
+5. Browser smoke proves v1 load, apply/cancel, keyboard limits and one renderer canvas. Integrated renderer quality, context/pipeline recovery and hardware performance remain finite runner obligations.
