+# Proposed migration patch and consumer seams
+
+`migration.patch` is an explicit proposal against the product settings paths, generated from exact control versus candidate bytes. It has not been applied to product code. It also proposes four immutable pure v1 oracle files under `src/settings/legacyV1` and changes the candidate's bound-control decoder import to that local path. Those files contain validation/preset/schema/types only; no second store/controller is instantiated.
+
+1. A0 reviews the patch at its own accepted source. Preserve the 19 v1 IDs, original bounds, defaults, preset mapping and `effectsQuality` decoration contract. New desired values are additive and independent. Decode v1 through the frozen validator, then add defaults; save writes v2 only after explicit Apply. Preserve unknown future bytes.
+2. Adopt `GraphicsSettingsV2` in `GraphicsRuntimePort.apply` and its consumers: `src/render/three/graphicsSettingsAdapter.ts`, `src/main.ts`, `src/render/three/debugScene.ts`, `src/ui/graphicsSettingsPanel.ts` and existing settings unit/E2E fixtures. The settings patch alone is not a completed product port and should not be merged as one. Product adapter factory owns context power preference and actual AA/power/backend reporting; changing these requests controlled restart, not a live device swap.
+3. Bring the pure `frameWindow.ts`, `quality.ts` and renderer `probe.ts` into the existing render telemetry/policy paths. Read metrics from actual renderer context/device; never install a probe canvas or infer memory/performance from names. Map `snapshot.eligible` to policy validity, pass actual capability revision/limits and carry returned scalar state. Use `confirmed.adaptiveResolution` as desired; never feed effective scale/DPR into draft or persisted display values.
+4. Apply returned transient `{renderScale,maxDevicePixelRatio}` through an explicit presentation-only renderer method. The integrated adapter must return its current snapshot after resize/context/restart and report unsupported pipelines honestly. Reference profiles freeze current quality. Resource pressure/admission remains exclusively S3's ledger, not this controller.
+5. Run the finite runner rest profile after A0 chooses integration, source/save/collision binding and a slot. Keep DOM HUD resolution separate. Required product regressions include all old settings assertions and E2E/live flows, world/save/collision parity and context/pipeline recovery. No automatic adoption, benchmark acceptance or main merge follows from the synthetic policy suite.
+
+`review-diff.patch` exports the complete new source/spec/test/fixture/report changes and binary smoke screenshots, excluding the private-path-bearing local diagnostic files listed in the seal. `seal.json` enumerates and hashes those retained originals as well as every exported file. Review them locally; do not publish private paths or unapproved artifacts. No approval is recorded by this proposal.
