+# GFX-01-02: isolated settings-v2-candidate
+
+Implementation COMPLETE; focused code/oracles PASS. LOCAL_WINDOWS_ISOLATED. CANDIDATE; product integration NO. Hardware/reference and integrated Hestia quality remain NOT_RUN.
+
+Hypothesis: extend the existing settings/store/renderer-port architecture with additive preferences and a small deterministic resolution policy, preserving every original setting and world/save/collision semantics. One control and one candidate; no new GraphicsStore, dependencies for hardware classification, ML policy or resource ledger.
+
+## Run
+
+From this directory under `C:\IFI_SourceCode`, use the verified Node22 `C:\IFI_SourceCode\Utils\npm-tmp\opencode\node-v22.23.2-win-x64\node.exe`.
+
+```powershell
+$node = 'C:\IFI_SourceCode\Utils\npm-tmp\opencode\node-v22.23.2-win-x64\node.exe'
+& $node seal.mjs --verify
+& $node repro.mjs
+$env:GFX_SERVE_MS='120000'
+& $node serve.mjs
+```
+
+Open `http://127.0.0.1:5192/`. Native Playwright runtime can execute `tests/browser-smoke.js` and `tests/browser-negative.js`; both are finite and verify the exact origin. They manipulate only the isolated demo-origin graphics key. The negative profile preserves and restores its prior fixture bytes. Server binds loopback only and exits after the configured finite duration. The UI loads an actual v1 envelope generated by the unchanged module when its demo key is missing; existing values are preserved.
+
+Clean installation, only in this spike: `node <pinned-node-dir>/node_modules/npm/bin/npm-cli.js ci --ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps --no-audit --no-fund --cache node_modules/.npm-cache`. npm 10.9.8 peer auto-resolution hit an Arborist `edgesOut` error; the successful lock uses legacy peer resolution. No package lifecycle scripts or product dependencies were changed. TypeScript 5.9.3 (Apache-2.0) and Vitest 4.1.11 (MIT) are exact pins; registry integrity, actual exports and transitive lock are bound by `dependencies.json` and `seal.json`. This compiler verifies the spike, not the product's TypeScript 7.0.2 build.
+
+## Contents and API
+
+- `control/**`: exact 17b1 source/test snapshots; `source-manifest.json` names every original path/hash. Four unchanged core suites pass 27/27. The original Three adapter/E2E/sampler are bound read-only context, not stubbed controls or executed integrated tests.
+- `settings-v2-candidate/src/settings/**`: existing ten-module architecture extended to v2. Adds rayTracing/weatherQuality/powerPreference/adaptiveResolution. Presets/effects keep old semantics. Confirmed desired and transient effective values stay separate; runtime apply failure retains confirmed desire and reports failure. Cancel discards only draft. Future schema bytes cannot be overwritten by Apply.
+- `src/frameWindow.ts`: bounded finite sample window, p50/p95, take/consume and continuity breaks. Missing/disjoint timings are null or ineligible. `src/quality.ts`: `decideQuality(metrics, desired, current, state) -> {quality,state,action,reason}`; no Three import, storage, source or solver access.
+- `src/probe.ts`: scalar evidence from the supplied renderer/context/device; actual versus available adapter, features/explicit limits, unknown memory and no second canvas. Adapter capability is not device-feature enablement or speed. Power is a hint. The UI is a static single WebGL context, not a Hestia scene renderer.
+- `MIGRATION.md`, `migration.patch`, `HANDOFF.md`, `runner-profile.json`: explicit A0 integration seams and finite rest checks. `seal.json` exhaustively binds dirty files and built bytes, including receipt and retained raw failures. Its sole self-exclusion is the seal envelope itself.
+
+Policy: minimum 30 samples and 400ms per non-overlapping window; three GPU-pressure windows reduce scale by 0.1, then DPR by 0.25. Eight reserve windows increase in reverse order. Cooldown 2000ms; gap over 2000ms resets streaks. Constants are a testable starting policy, not reference-device thresholds. Manual and capability bounds are exact even for fractions; disabled automation preserves fixed user values apart from hardware ceilings. Freeze prevents quality changes; exceeding a frozen capability requests reprofile. CPU pressure never causes repeated pixel reduction.
+
+Fps target is an adaptive presentation budget independent of the existing `fpsLimit` scheduler; the integrated caller must sample presented frames and choose compatible target/limiter values. S3 owns all resource admission. No quality value writes to canonical world/save/source/collision state.
+
+The global DevToolbox verify profile still targets read-only product dependencies and records MODULE_NOT_FOUND. Completion preflight is advisory and can proceed; focused evidence suffices for this spike. This does not turn the global check green. See REPORT for exact evidence boundaries.
