+`tests/final-functional.json` contains real exit codes: configured Vitest 4.1.11, 10 files / 74 tests, Node22 v22.23.2; TypeScript 5.9.3 typecheck/build both exit 0. Four unchanged baseline suites remain 27/27. `source-manifest.json` binds all 19 copied inputs to 17b1db4201a28e7b607c30707bdc2b75e3484a10. The 12 hand-authored fixtures include all eight requested sequence families; their expected complete arrays are not derived from the implementation. Fixture SHA256 stayed `567f8fff023a7efc28081cc9ba1045e11d9a9533209258eb5b2e704d15b6faba` across review repairs.
+
+`tests/browser-results.json` and `browser-negative-results.json` record actual browser 155.0.8059.40. The smoke used 1100x850 and 360x780 DOM viewports; observed DPR 1.25. WebGL2 used ANGLE Intel Arc Pro 140T, Direct3D11. WebGPU adapter was available, separately labelled; no WebGPU device or render pass was created. Timer capability was available, but no GPU time was measured (`gpuTimeMs:null`). Actual GPU memory remains unknown. The browser warned that requestAdapter powerPreference is currently ignored on Windows; it is never treated as a guaranteed adapter selection. Three screenshots are functional smoke only, not Hestia image-quality/art approval.
+
+Context-loss injection in the lab preserved the last effective scale, reported Unsupported capabilities and an unavailable warning after Apply. Future-version bytes survived explicit Apply unchanged. These are real small-browser negative cases; they do not qualify Hestia pipeline/context recovery. Browser source imports and forbidden server paths were checked with real HTTP responses. The initial server import failures and raw test failures remain preserved.
+
+## Review and failures
+
+Read-only reviewer found fractional clamp rounding, lost continuity through short hidden/warmup/backend boundaries, a wrong WebGPU default enum, decimal form-step incompatibility, lost-context apply reporting and stale effective metadata after external resize/restart. All were repaired; explicit red-to-green regressions are retained. Final bounded review has no open findings. `tests/REVIEW.md` records the boundary. No independent hardware review or human Plannotator approval is claimed.
+
+Initial sandbox npm requests failed ENOTFOUND, followed by npm 10 Arborist optional-peer `edgesOut`; scoped install succeeded with `--ignore-scripts --legacy-peer-deps`. Initial Vitest temp renames failed EPERM; process-local TMP/TEMP under the spike fixed the execution location. Original raw diagnostic bytes remain local; no global settings, caches or services were patched.
+
+The DevToolbox workspace verifier ran Specs PASS (exit 0) and the inherited product typecheck FAIL (exit 1 / MODULE_NOT_FOUND), because product `node_modules/typescript` is absent. Installing there or changing the root verify profile is outside this task. The exact result is retained under this change's tests. Completion preflight is advisory (`canProceed:true`, no blockers); the manual decision accepts the fresh focused evidence for spike task closure while preserving the inherited failure. It does not qualify the product build.
+
+## Boundaries
+
+No measured FPS benefit, GPU-pass threshold, preferred-NVIDIA selection, image equivalence, workload isolation, hardware/reference PASS or cross-device PASS. No Unity/product/solver/save/source/collision edits, resource budget authority, 42/1400 series, commit, push, merge or publication. The spike has no custom shader or game-WASM input; explicit NOT_APPLICABLE bindings are in the seal. Integrated rest checks are finite and manual in runner-profile.json.
+
+API evidence checked against primary references: [WebGPU power enum](https://gpuweb.github.io/types/types/GPUPowerPreference.html), [GPUAdapter properties](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/GPUAdapter) and [WebGL timer specification](https://registry.khronos.org/webgl/extensions/EXT_disjoint_timer_query_webgl2/). Capability/feature availability is not timing or hardware qualification.
